*   **Installation:** Ensure you have Mongoose in your project: `npm install --save mongoose`

**2. Schema Composition with Nested Objects**

   The core technique is nesting schemas within your main schema to represent the multiple data types efficiently.

   ```typescript
   import { Prop, Schema, SchemaFactory } from '@nestjs/mongoose';
   import { Document, Types } from 'mongoose';

   // Interface for User Profile (Schema 1)
   interface UserProfile {
       name: string;
       email: string;
       bio: string;
   }

   // Interface for Project Details (Schema 2)
   interface ProjectDetails {
       title: string;
       technologies: string[];
       startDate: Date;
       status: 'ongoing' | 'completed';
   }

   // Main Model Schema
   @Schema({ timestamps: true }) // Add createdAt, updatedAt fields
   export class User extends Document {
       @Prop({ required: true })
       _id: Types.ObjectId; 

       @Prop({ type: Schema.Types.Object })
       profile: UserProfile; 

       @Prop({ type: Schema.Types.Array })
       projects: ProjectDetails[]; 
   }

   export const UserSchema = SchemaFactory.createForClass(User);
   ```

